# Configuration Guide

<aside>
💡

ℹ️ This guide provides step-by-step instructions for configuring Ignite Video in different configurations and explains their respective privacy implications. Because Ignite does not process personal data of website visitors, **no configuration in the Consenter Manager is required or applicable.**

**Step 1:** Choose which configuration matches your requirements and configure Ignite accordingly.

**Step 2:** No configuration in the Consenter Manager is required. Ignite does not need to be registered as a data recipient in your consent banner.

**Step 3:** Explain how you use Ignite in your **privacy policy**.

</aside>

<aside>
💡

⚠️ **No Consent Banner Required**

Ignite Video is designed from the ground up as a privacy-first, cookie-free, and consent-free video hosting platform. When delivering video content on your website, **Ignite does not collect, store, or process any personal data from your website visitors.**

**As a result, no entry for Ignite needs to be created in the Consenter Manager, and no consent banner configuration is required for Ignite.** Ignite-embedded videos are displayed to all visitors regardless of their consent status, including those who have declined all cookies.

</aside>

Ignite Video (ignite.video) is a European video hosting and streaming platform operated by Ignite Video GmbH, headquartered in Düsseldorf, Germany. It allows website operators to embed and deliver video content directly on their websites without setting cookies or processing personal data of visitors. Unlike platforms such as YouTube or Vimeo, Ignite is built on a privacy-by-design architecture: no tracking scripts are loaded, no fingerprinting takes place, and no identifiers are assigned to viewers. All infrastructure — including the video encoding pipeline and CDN — is hosted in Europe (Germany and France). An optional first-party domain feature (available from the "Grow" package onwards) allows videos to be delivered via the operator's own subdomain, making Ignite's involvement entirely invisible to the end user and to ad blockers.

