## Step 1 — Ignite Configuration

| # | Configuration Area | Where in Ignite | Configuration A — Standard (Third-Party Domain) | Configuration B — First-Party Domain |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Video delivery domain | Account Settings → Custom Domain | Videos delivered via Ignite's own CDN domain (e.g. `play.ignite.video`) | Videos delivered via operator's own subdomain (e.g. `videos.yourdomain.com`) via DNS entry |
| 2 | Cookie usage | Platform-level (not configurable by operator) | No cookies set — by design | No cookies set — by design |
| 3 | Personal data collection from viewers | Platform-level (not configurable by operator) | None — no IP addresses, no fingerprinting, no behavioural data collected or stored | None — no IP addresses, no fingerprinting, no behavioural data collected or stored |
| 4 | Video analytics | Account Settings → Analytics | Aggregate, anonymised video statistics (play counts, completion rates) — no personal data | Aggregate, anonymised video statistics (play counts, completion rates) — no personal data |
| 5 | Processing location | Platform-level | EU (Germany/France) — Scalingo SAS (Strasbourg) and 3DS OUTSCALE SAS (Saint-Cloud) as sub-processors | EU (Germany/France) — Scalingo SAS (Strasbourg) and 3DS OUTSCALE SAS (Saint-Cloud) as sub-processors; CDN delivery via operator's own domain |
| 6 | Data processing agreement (DPA) | Available on request from Ignite | Available — contact hallo@ignite.video | Available — contact hallo@ignite.video |

### Configuration A — Standard (Third-Party Domain)

Use this configuration when embedding Ignite videos on your website using the default Ignite CDN domain (`play.ignite.video` or similar). In this configuration, Ignite handles all video delivery from its own infrastructure. No cookies are set on your visitors' browsers, and no personal data is collected from viewers at any point — not even temporarily. The video player loads and streams content without performing any fingerprinting, storing any identifiers, or logging IP addresses. Video analytics provided within the Ignite dashboard are fully anonymised and aggregated (e.g. total play counts and completion rates); they cannot be used to identify individual viewers. All processing takes place in the EU (Germany and France), with Scalingo SAS and 3DS OUTSCALE SAS acting as sub-processors under their respective DPAs. Because no personal data of website visitors is processed, no legal basis for processing under the GDPR is required, and no consent banner entry for Ignite is needed.

Note that although some server-level log data (such as IP addresses used for CDN delivery) may be processed transiently in the course of delivering the video stream, Ignite explicitly states that it does not store or retain any such data. This position has been confirmed in Ignite's legal review by Heidrich Lawyers.

### Configuration B — First-Party Domain

Use this configuration when delivering Ignite videos via your own subdomain (e.g. `videos.yourdomain.com`), which requires a one-time DNS entry in your domain settings. Available from Ignite's "Grow" package onwards. In this configuration, the Ignite infrastructure is entirely invisible to your visitors, to search engines, and to ad blockers, as all video content appears to originate from your own domain. From a privacy perspective, this configuration is equivalent to Configuration A: no cookies are set, no personal data is collected from viewers, and all processing remains in the EU. The first-party domain setup provides additional practical benefits — such as improved SEO, bypassing corporate firewalls, and preventing ad-blocker interference — but it does not alter the underlying data protection position. No consent banner entry is required.

