## Step 2 — Mapping in the Consenter Manager

**No configuration in the Consenter Manager is required for Ignite Video.**

Because Ignite does not process any personal data of your website visitors, there is no data processing activity that would require consent under the GDPR or the ePrivacy Directive. Ignite does not set cookies or comparable tracking technologies, and no personal data is transferred to Ignite as a result of a visitor viewing a video on your website.

This assessment is supported by a legal review conducted by Heidrich Lawyers, which concluded: *"no data protection consent or documentation obligations are required in relation to cookies. Since no technically necessary cookies are required, there is no need to inform the user about the use of cookies or to use corresponding cookie banners."*

As a result, Ignite should not be listed as a data recipient in your consent banner, and no tracking, identifier, or data category selections need to be made in the Consenter Manager for this service.

