## Step 3 — Privacy Policy

Although no consent banner entry is required, you should briefly reference Ignite in your website's privacy policy for the sake of transparency. Ignite provides GDPR text templates for this purpose (available from your Ignite account or on request). The following information should be included:

- The name of the service (Ignite Video) and the operator (Ignite Video GmbH, Düsseldorf, Germany)
- The purpose of use (video hosting and delivery)
- A statement that Ignite does not set cookies and does not collect personal data from visitors
- The processing location (EU — Germany/France)
- A reference to Ignite's privacy policy: https://www.ignite.video/en/privacy

> **Note:** If you also use Ignite's optional video analytics feature, you may wish to mention that aggregated, anonymised viewing statistics are generated. As these do not involve personal data, no legal basis or consent is required for this either.
